data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"Task for you (dev), on your clone of the subject repository, on your own branch.\\n\\nImplement exactly this:\\n\\n1. Create `src/greet.py` with a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` where `\u003cname\u003e` is the `name` argument interpolated in\\n   (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. Create `tests/test_greet.py` with unit tests (using the `unittest` module)\\n   that cover:\\n   - a normal name, e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - the empty string, e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n3. Verify locally that `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (no\\n   failures, no errors) before you commit.\\n\\n4. Commit both files to your own branch. Do not touch any other files.\\n\\n5. Reply with an honest summary: what you implemented, the exact output of\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`, and confirm the commit is on your\\n   branch.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

